Statement of Purpose

The laws of most jurisdictions throughout the world automatically confer exclusive Copyright and Related Rights (defined below) upon the creator and subsequent owner(s).

Each owner of Copyright and Related Rights is interested in a universal, permanent, free and irrevocable waiver of all such rights, and a dedication of the work to the public domain, to the fullest extent permitted by law, so that the work may be freely reproduced, distributed, adapted, performed, displayed, compiled and otherwise exploited, in whole or in part, for any purpose and by any means, without any restrictions, including but not limited to copyright and related rights, database rights, moral rights, publicity and privacy rights, and any other rights similar to any of the foregoing (hereinafter, "Copyright and Related Rights").

A person who applies CC0 to a work (the "Affirmer") waives all Copyright and Related Rights in the work, to the fullest extent permitted by law, and dedicates the work to the public domain. If such waiver is not legally permissible, CC0 acts as a license from the Affirmer granting a perpetual, irrevocable, royalty‑free, non‑exclusive, worldwide license to reproduce, adapt, distribute, perform, display, compile and otherwise exploit the work for any purpose, including commercial purposes, without any separate permission.

CC0 is intended for use with works that are not already in the public domain in their entirety, such as works that are still protected by copyright or related rights.

For the full official legal text, see https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
